I can't calculate 2025 gross margin from the data I have. Gross margin is (revenue − cost of goods sold) / revenue. The tables cover marketing spend (ads, CTV, email, partner fees, webinars), CRM leads and opportunities, and sales headcount. None of them hold COGS, such as hosting, support or delivery costs. Marketing and sales costs are operating expenses, so they don't belong in gross margin. Any figure I gave would be an estimate, and I'd have to invent a definition of COGS to get it.

If you can give me a COGS or gross-margin source, or tell me which costs count as COGS, I can work it out.

